    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32491" root="غن" body-key="g">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غنّنهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغْنِينٌ</span>, <i>It rendered him</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغَنّ</span>
[q. v.]. (K.) One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَدْرِى مَا غَنَّنَهُ</span> <i>I know
not what rendered him,</i> or <i>has rendered him</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغَنّ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غنّن صَوْتَهُ</span> <i>He made his
voice to have in it a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُنَّة</span> [q. v.]. (Mughnee, art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرْفُ النُّونِ</span>. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغَنٍّ</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَنَّآءٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غنى</span>.])

